    rdf:value """wonderful creature? He feels as wretched over it as everyone who cares for her does, but he had more reason than most, for he knows how poor she is, and how her mother is selling all her property and using up the money.
Clayton Jones told us how Mrs. Gardner entertained the Thursday Evening Club in the depths of winter, with no fires. Everyone was shivering and some one said she had put the last touch to her decorations by adding “a frieze of eminent Bostonians.”
In the evening we dined with the Longyears and listened to more of that horrible drivel about Christian Science. But Mrs. Longyear is so genial and nice, she almost carries it off. She has a great sense of fun, too. She told us of a man who came to a “Healer” to be cured of the """^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 73 ;
